    "id": 805892,
    "name": "Pickling Cucumber",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">These picklers get chubby quick, but retain great flavor as they grow so you may get a range of sizes. You don't have to pickle picklers. Harvested young, when the seed cavities are small, any variety of pickler is fine for fresh eating in a salad or out of hand. Pickler varieties aren't uniformly dark green like the slicing-type cucumbers sold in the supermarket. They are paler green, sometimes with light-colored stripes running lengthwise down the fruit. Picklers have thinner skin and crisper, crunchier flesh than most slicers.</span></p>",
